  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="2">1. Differentia inter legata &amp; fideicommissa</l>
    <l n="3">proponitur.</l>
    <l n="4">2. Ea sublata jure posteriori.</l>
    <l n="5">3. Aliqua tamen in re &amp; verbis superest</l>
    <l n="6">differentia.</l>
    <l n="7">4. Objectio removetur.</l>
    <l n="8" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="9">1. Res omnes legari possunt.</l>
    <l n="10">2. Quædam res, &amp; facta legari non possunt.</l>
    <l n="11">3. Ubi legatum rei prorsus est inutile ibi ne</l>
    <l n="12">quidem debetur æstimatio.</l>
    <l n="13">4. Casu quo statutum prohibet immobilia</l>
    <l n="14">legari, nec debebitur æstimatio.</l>
    <l n="15">5. Idem quod in feudo legato obtinet.</l>
    <l n="16">6. Res alterius legari potest.</l>
    <l n="17">7. Quid obtineat jure Canonum?</l>
    <l n="18" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 5.</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">Res obligata recte legatur, &amp; quis eam</l>
    <l n="20">luat, explicatur.</l>
    <l n="21" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 6.</l>
    <l n="22">1. Rei quæ facta est legatarii, legatum valet.</l>
    <l n="23">2. Eadem quantitas multoties relicta, forte</l>
    <l n="24">nonnisi semel debebitur.</l>
    <l n="25" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 7.</l>
    <l n="26" para="true">Quod non est, legari quandoque potest.</l>
    <l n="27" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 8.</l>
    <l n="28">1. Eadem res duobus legari potest.</l>
    <l n="29">2. Explicatur jus accrescendi.</l>
    <l n="30">3. Quod moribus cessat.</l>
    <l n="31" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 9.</l>
    <l n="32" para="true">Fundi proprietas sola legari potest, &amp;</l>
    <l n="33">quid obtineat illo casu.</l>
    <l n="34" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 10.</l>
    <l n="35" para="true">Res legatarii quandoque ei legari potest.</l>
    <l n="36" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 11.</l>
    <l n="37">1. Veritas opinioni præfertur.</l>
    <l n="38">2. Non semper tamen.</l>
    <l n="39" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 12.</l>
    <l n="40" para="true">Legatum debetur, nisi fuerit ademptum.</l>
    <l n="41" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 13.</l>
    <l n="42">1. Liberatio legari potest debitori.</l>
    <l n="43">2. Non actio in rem.</l>
    <l n="44">3. Moribus qui legetur debitum?</l>
    <l n="45" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 14.</l>
    <l n="46">1. Creditori quod debet testator legare potest.</l>
    <l n="47">2. Non tamen si debitor certam quantitatem leget creditori, compensandi animus præsumitur.</l>
    <l n="48">3. Difficultas aliqua tollitur.</l>
    <l n="49" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 15.</l>
    <l n="50">1. Legatum dotis valet.</l>
    <l n="51">2. Non semper tamen.</l>
    <l n="52">3. Jure Saxonico quid obtineat?</l>
    <l n="53" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 16.</l>
    <l n="54" para="true">Cui pereat res legata?</l>
    <l n="55" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 17.</l>
    <l n="56" para="true">Legatum cum accessione debetur.</l>
    <l n="57" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 18.</l>
    <l n="58">1. Quale sit legatum gregis, &amp; quadrigæ?</l>
    <l n="59">2. Quid moribus?</l>
    <l n="60" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 19.</l>
    <l n="61" para="true">Quale legatum adimum?</l>
    <l n="62" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 20.</l>
    <l n="63">1. Quale legatum peculii?</l>
    <l n="64">2. Servum manumissum non sequitur.</l>
    <l n="65" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 21.</l>
    <l n="66">1. Actiones legari poterunt.</l>
    <l n="67">2. Quando pereat actionum legatum?</l>
    <l n="68" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 22.</l>
    <l n="69">1. Electio cui competat?</l>
    <l n="70">2. Quid moribus?</l>
    <l n="71" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 23.</l>
    <l n="72">1. Optio ab electione distinguitur.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Printed in two columns; the layout of section numbers is reconstructed. Some words are doubtful in the scan, notably "adimum" (likely "adimi") and "Liberatio legari potest" (possibly "legari"). Page is a contents/summary page of the book's material index.</notes>
